# World 2's patrol boats from mission 5 (decided by Paul, 2026-11-13; SPEC 6): Ctrl+L, W, 5 starts
# mission 5 at the base pad. The patrol boat sails the stretch of sea just west of the base island
# (x 3620-3960): take off, fly low toward it and hover there, and its bow gun swings up with the
# lamp lit (the tell, 4 frames longer than a gunboat's), then a shell, and only then. Mission 4's
# patrol boats never shoot (tests/w2patrol4.agk); the unit tests (tests/unit/test_logic.c,
# testW2Patrol*) hold the rules: the tell table, no shot at a high chopper, from off screen,
# point-blank, out of sight or just after take-off, the landed grace, one attack at a time.
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x05
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 700
press fire 2
wait 40
press up 20
press left 80
wait 60
screenshot low
wait-serial "boat tell" 900
screenshot tell
wait-serial "boat fire" 60
wait 5
screenshot fire
expect-serial "boat tell[\s\S]*boat fire"
expect-no-serial "chopper lost|ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 90
expect-min-chip-free 96
